443	82,1262,315,1664	443. Flower of Garden Sage.	A Garden Sage flower seen from the side: a two-lipped corolla with a hooded, arching upper lip and a spreading lower lip, standing in its pointed tubular calyx.
444	205,1135,435,1664 - 205,1225,314,1670	444. Pistil of the same, the 4-lobed ovary in the bottom of the calyx, half of which is cut away.	The Sage pistil standing in the calyx, half of which is cut away: the four-lobed ovary at the bottom sends up one very long style that arches over and ends in a forked tip.
